Constructs a Merkle tree yielding one checksum for all container data. Chunk checksums (leaves) aggregate all per-chunk checksums; block checksums aggregate chunk checksums (sorted by offset); the container checksum aggregates block checksums (sorted by block ID). Uses CRC32C for all tree-level aggregation regardless of the underlying data's checksum algorithm. It builds incrementally via `addChunks(...)` and only computes the higher-level checksums when `toProto()` is called. It contains two private static inner classes, `BlockMerkleTreeWriter` and `ChunkMerkleTreeWriter`.

